@startuml 04-solution-event-decomposition
!theme plain
title Proposed Solution A: Event-Based Decomposition of finalizeOrder()

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle frame

package "Current: Monolithic finalizeOrder()" #FFCDD2 {
    [finalizeOrder()] as Mono
    note right of Mono
        Single method doing:
        - Validation
        - Order creation
        - Payment execution
        - Number assignment
        - Notifications
        **Problem: Cant customize individual steps**
    end note
}

package "Proposed: Event-Driven Order Creation" #C8E6C9 {
    package "Events" #E8F5E9 {
        [OrderCreationRequestedEvent] as E1
        [OrderValidatedEvent] as E2
        [OrderPersistedEvent] as E3
        [PaymentProcessedEvent] as E4
        [OrderNumberAssignedEvent] as E5
        [OrderCompletedEvent] as E6
    }

    package "Handlers" #F5F5F5 {
        [OrderValidationHandler] as H1
        [OrderPersistenceHandler] as H2
        [PaymentExecutionHandler] as H3
        [OrderNumberHandler] as H4
        [NotificationHandler] as H5
        [VoucherHandler] as H6
    }

    E1 --> H1 : validates basket/user/delivery
    H1 --> E2 : if valid

    E2 --> H2 : creates order record
    H2 --> E3 : after save

    E3 --> H3 : executes payment gateway
    note right of H3
        For Stripe:
        Handler is SKIPPED or returns immediately
        (payment already processed)
    end note
    H3 --> E4 : after payment

    E4 --> H4 : assigns order number
    H4 --> E5 : after number set

    E5 --> H5 : sends emails
    E5 --> H6 : marks vouchers
    H5 --> E6 : after notifications
    H6 --> E6 : after vouchers
}

note as Benefits
    **Advantages of Event-Driven:**

    1. Testable - Each handler tested in isolation
    2. Extensible - Add/remove handlers without modifying core
    3. Customizable - Stripe skips PaymentExecutionHandler
    4. Observable - Log/monitor each step
    5. Recoverable - Retry individual steps on failure
end note

note as Strategy
    **For Stripe Module (without core changes):**

    Create wrapper service that:
    1. Emits custom pre-events before finalizeOrder()
    2. Calls finalizeOrder() with overridden Order model
    3. Emits custom post-events after finalizeOrder()

    This gives us extension points without
    breaking OXID core or other modules.
end note

Benefits -[hidden]- Strategy

@enduml
